    "problem": "Historically planted shelter belts often failed because their narrow, single-species design made them highly vulnerable to being destroyed by winter gales, which negated their intended protective benefits for stock and crops.",
    "method": "The paper describes an investigation of wind, temperature, humidity, and other microclimatic factors to determine general conclusions on effective shelter-belt types, lay-out, and structure for the protection of stock and crops.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the influences of shelter belts on microclimate, soil moisture, and precipitation, assessing their economic significance and providing conclusions on optimal shelter-belt types, layout, and structure.",
